# proxmox-backup-client

This stow package contains the statically 
linked binaries of two files:

- `proxmox-backup` client; version `4.0.14`
  * used for when access to the **PBS** server
  repository is accessible -- this is typically
  the preferred route, but is not always going
  to be the case!
- `pxar`; version `4.0.14`
  * used for when we are restoring files off
  of our offsite backup disks.

I have created this package for the sake of 
being prepared in case of disaster striking --
better safe than sorry!

The binary files found here are extracted from the
[Debian Trixie repository][20].

## usage

- [[../proxmox-backup/README.stow]]

### setup

```shell
# assuming we already have the dotfiles.git repo
# checked out and at the right branch
stow -Rv proxmox-backup-client

# now, you should find the two binaries here:
~/local/sbin/proxmox-backup-client --help
~/local/sbin/pxar --help
```

